                <pb facs="0490" n="378" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg378"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Minister Dawson.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1909-03-17"><hi rendition="#italic">March 17,
                        1909</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Your telegram of March 16, 5 p.m., received. You may informally express to
                    President Reyes our cordial sympathy and our confidence that he will do all
                    possible to bring about the approval of the treaties, and thus consummate the
                    good relationship we so earnestly desire.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Knox.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
